  "definition": "Epinephrine is a hormone released by the adrenal medulla that activates both major adrenergic receptor systems. It boosts cardiac activity, tightens blood vessels in much of the body, relaxes the digestive tract, and opens the airways and blood vessels supplying the brain.",
